Subject: [PATCH 10/10] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 4, patch 10;
 built on 87bfa1f05 with series 3 and the first nine patches of series 4
 applied): A RECORDED ACT DOES NOT BREAK THE LOCKS. The rule of series 2, and
 the fourth patch of this series, ask main to record an act by name in the
 gates: what left a ledger in LEFT_BY_NAME, what rose in RAISED_BY_NAME. Seven
 tests of two locks record such an act in a small repository of their own.
 They planted it by rewriting the text of an empty table, so they held only
 while nothing was named on this repository: the first act main recorded would
 have failed each of the seven, for no fault of a gate. Found on 2026-11-12,
 when main first had an act to record: two tests left their locks in the mends
 of Review 79, and the fourth patch's rule asks for their record. The fault is
 the seat's, and part of it is in the lock of series 2, which is on main. THE
 MEND is in the two locks only; no gate and no checker is changed. The table
 is found by the statement that binds it, in the syntax tree, and the entry is
 added on the line after it, to whatever the table holds. AND A RECORDED ACT
 IS SAID IN THE LOCK ONCE. The two tests that compare a table whole with what
 the lock knows of it stay as they are: they are where main says what it
 records, in the same commit. Three more tests read this repository, one for
 the two pages, one for the locks, one for the tests of the locks; each also
 held the gate's note to be empty, so that one recorded act would have had to
 be said in two or three tests. They now hold what they are about: nothing has
 left without a record, and a note stands only where the table holds a record
 for that ledger. No test is taken out or renamed, and each change carries a
 dated note. The test that compares LEFT_BY_NAME keeps the name it had on the
 day the table was empty: a test that is renamed has left its lock. What the
 patch does not do: it records nothing. The two tests that left are main's to
 record; until they are, the vacuity gate and two tests of these locks are red
 on main's head, by the rule and not by this fault. The lock: one test added
 to tests/test_nothing_leaves_a_ledger.py and one to
 tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py, which run the seven on a copy of
 the gates in which each table already holds an act, written over several
 lines as main would write one. Added to the two locks as they stood on the
 commit before, both fail: seven of the seven tests that record an act fail
 there, each on its count of an empty table. Tested against planted errors, 7
 of 7; computed once. 0 of 19.

